    "text": "Body: 1-junction of the lunar module. Inertia = modulated spatial I (m(t), J(m)); Out1..6 = MR on the joint's drive axes (1-junctions Axis1..6), r = -dm/dt and -dJ/dt: the propellant that leaves takes its momentum with it.",
    "x": 400,
    "y": 60,
    "w": 560,
    "h": 60
   },
   {
    "id": "a2",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "Apollo 11 ascent from Tranquility Base to orbit insertion: the ascent stage lifts off the descent stage (which stays behind), rises vertically, pitches over and flies Apollo's linear guidance to 60,000 ft, 5,535 ft/s; the ascent engine is cut on the target velocity.",
    "x": 40,
    "y": -40,
    "w": 960,
    "h": 60
   }
  ]
